                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "da33b367-35b6-40aa-8775-51e23716c00c",
                        "source_entry_id": "1d584b21-e090-3b93-9fb8-d69dcd6221d6",
                        "source_sense_id": "bf93bfff-ff76-3b5e-88cc-c395e16c9715",
                        "source_sense_description": "männlicher Vorname",
                        "target_lang_word": "Christopher",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Christopher",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a27f2698-7900-383c-909f-7d960fc08218",
                                        "entry_id": "2cae04e2-890c-3831-a645-56232c500872",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A male given name from Ancient Greek."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86019a73-9ae5-4232-bccf-4bcd24b85c30",
                                                "sense_id": "a27f2698-7900-383c-909f-7d960fc08218",
                                                "text": "Am not I Christopher Sly, old Sly's son, of Burtonheath; by birth a pedlar, by education a card-maker, by transmutation a bear-herd, and now by present profession a tinker?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2eab3d44-6851-4658-aef3-75a9696be4d6",
                                                "sense_id": "a27f2698-7900-383c-909f-7d960fc08218",
                                                "text": "- - - a baby, which also happened to fall due, was baptized \"Paul\" ( for the church ) \"Christopher\" ( because St. Christopher had to do with rivers and ferries ), the Rector strenuously resisting the parents' desire to call it \"Van Weyden Flood\"."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4eb6c94e-6e73-4a86-8ae8-f7cebe9848b2",
                                                "sense_id": "a27f2698-7900-383c-909f-7d960fc08218",
                                                "text": "A similar impulse sometimes accompanies my reading of the work of Christopher F. Rufo, a fellow at the Manhattan Institute and one of the most gifted conservative polemicists of his generation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "91a3db19-8385-3b15-9fe8-facb42a586bc",
                                        "entry_id": "2cae04e2-890c-3831-a645-56232c500872",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A surname originating as a patronymic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ae21a307-1ef7-45d5-9483-fd34e01e339b",
                        "source_entry_id": "1d584b21-e090-3b93-9fb8-d69dcd6221d6",
                        "source_sense_id": "bf93bfff-ff76-3b5e-88cc-c395e16c9715",
                        "source_sense_description": "männlicher Vorname",
                        "target_lang_word": "Christophe",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Christophe",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d3b9193c-24ed-3287-a150-a2f2d0ddc795",
                                        "entry_id": "7cb845b7-f044-33f3-87c2-8ee8f6370798",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Prénom masculin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "23503ea9-257f-4be5-b258-252dd4f73742",
                                                "sense_id": "d3b9193c-24ed-3287-a150-a2f2d0ddc795",
                                                "text": "Ainsi le voyageur, sur la terre d’Afrique, quoi qu’il fasse et quoi qu’il veuille, est toujours Christophe avec son long bâton, portant, auprès de sa tête inclinée, l’Enfant avec le globe et l’auréole de lumière invisible."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd195fc2-3d1c-46f7-86f5-dc4a331139a6",
                                                "sense_id": "d3b9193c-24ed-3287-a150-a2f2d0ddc795",
                                                "text": "« Vient qui veut, quel que soit son bord politique. La démarche est apartisane », présente Christophe Cassou, climatologue au CNRS et auteur du Groupe intergouvernemental du climat (Giec)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "88dd1b6d-9586-402d-ba14-6b89f2ff3fbd",
                                                "sense_id": "d3b9193c-24ed-3287-a150-a2f2d0ddc795",
                                                "text": "Le duo saintais a terminé en queue de peloton de l’épreuve où les candidats affrontaient le chef Christophe Renou, en fabriquant un gâteau sans moule."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "90ec68bf-3bd6-46c4-a45e-0b804c4e8a86",
                                                "sense_id": "d3b9193c-24ed-3287-a150-a2f2d0ddc795",
                                                "text": "À l’époque, Christophe avait aussi une histoire avec la petite Charlotte Brassard, si mignonne et clean en comparaison."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
